## End User License Agreement

This End User License Agreement (the "EULA") governs the installation, access, execution, and use of any local system application, installer, update, downloadable file, license key, activation information, documentation, or related software material provided by iisacc (collectively, the "Software"). By installing, executing, accessing, downloading, copying, or otherwise using the Software, the User is deemed to have read, understood, and agreed to this EULA.

If the User does not agree to this EULA, the User must not install, execute, access, download, copy, retain, or use the Software.

## License Grant and Permitted Scope

Subject to the User's continued compliance with this EULA, iisacc grants the User a limited, personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable license to install and use the Software only for the User's own lawful internal or personal purposes and only through the delivery, activation, and use methods expressly provided by iisacc.

Unless iisacc expressly states otherwise in a product-specific notice or separate written agreement, the license does not permit enterprise deployment, managed-service use, resale, rental, time-sharing, service bureau use, public hosting, use by multiple unrelated users, or use for the benefit of a third party. Any license quantity, device limit, user limit, term, product edition, access period, or feature restriction stated at purchase, delivery, activation, or inside the Software forms part of the permitted scope.

## Ownership and Reserved Rights

The Software is protected by copyright, trade secret, trademark, unfair competition, and other intellectual property and proprietary rights. iisacc and its licensors retain all rights, title, and interests in and to the Software, including source code, object code, executable files, architecture, user interface, visual assets, documentation, product identity, delivery flow, license systems, and all related materials.

No ownership right is transferred to the User. No right is granted by implication, estoppel, exhaustion, purchase, download, possession, or use. All rights not expressly granted in this EULA are reserved by iisacc and the relevant rights holders.

## Local System Responsibility

The Software may operate as a local system application on the User's own device, operating system, storage, files, settings, workflows, and third-party software environment. The User is solely responsible for determining whether the Software is suitable for the User's device, data, system configuration, security posture, intended use, and operational environment.

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, iisacc assumes no ex post responsibility or continuing responsibility for damage, loss, malfunction, incompatibility, data loss, interruption, security issue, user-created output, third-party conflict, system change, or any other consequence arising after delivery, installation, execution, configuration, or use of a local system application, except where liability cannot be excluded by mandatory law.

## System Requirements, Backups, and User Data

The User is responsible for reviewing any stated system requirements, supported operating systems, dependencies, storage requirements, permissions, and known limitations before installing or using the Software. The User is also responsible for maintaining backups of files, projects, settings, local databases, exports, and any other data that may be opened, generated, modified, or affected while using the Software.

iisacc does not guarantee restoration, recovery, compatibility, migration, preservation, or continued readability of User data, files, settings, outputs, or project materials. The User should verify important results independently and retain original files or separate backups before using the Software in any workflow where loss or alteration of data may matter.

