iisacc may provide, modify, delay, suspend, or discontinue updates, patches, installers, versions, features, activation methods, compatibility support, documentation, download links, or related services at its discretion, unless a separate written agreement expressly states otherwise. iisacc does not guarantee that any particular version, feature, download link, installer, update, activation method, or support path will remain available permanently.

Updates may change, add, remove, replace, or disable features. Continued use of the Software after an update, reinstall, replacement installer, or revised delivery method may be conditioned on acceptance of the EULA and policies then in effect. The User is responsible for deciding whether to install updates and for preserving any environment needed to continue using older files or workflows.

## Support and Maintenance

Support, maintenance, troubleshooting, bug fixes, updates, compatibility work, and documentation are provided only to the extent expressly stated by iisacc. Unless iisacc separately agrees otherwise, support is provided on a best-effort basis and does not guarantee a response within a particular time, resolution of all issues, continued support for any operating system or device, or addition of any requested feature.

The User must provide accurate, lawful, and reasonably complete information when requesting support. iisacc may refuse or limit support where the issue arises from unsupported environments, unauthorized modification, abnormal installation, license violation, third-party software or hardware, missing reproduction steps, abusive communication, or information that cannot reasonably be verified.

## No Personal Information Collection or Storage

The Software is provided on the premise that it does not collect, transmit, store, or maintain personal information through iisacc-operated systems. The Software does not create an iisacc-managed account database, user profile database, telemetry profile, cloud storage space, or personal information repository for the purpose of identifying or tracking the User.

Any information that remains on the User's local device, including files, settings, project data, caches, logs, exports, or operating-system-level records, is under the User's control and responsibility unless iisacc expressly states otherwise in a separate product-specific notice.

